# REDZ LKM614.
# Standard firmware with the OBIS_EURO list (24 values per meter). Other firmware (OBIS_EURO_1..14, TRF, 64-register
# versions) keeps the same addresses but maps different OBIS codes, so the names below would be wrong for it.
# Data addresses: the manual's table lists them as 1, 3, 5... (1-based), while its Modbus Poll and ZTerminal examples read
# Time at wire address 0 and 1.8.0 at 4. This map follows the examples. The settings (128-133) and monitoring (160-189)
# addresses are wire addresses, as the FC06/FC16 examples show.
# Values are the read-out digits without the decimal point, so no scale or unit is given: they depend on the meter.
# Mode switch 1 (OFF-OFF): 19200 8N1 on the Modbus side, 300 baud auto-switching on the meter side.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=REDZ
@vendor_website=redz-sc.com
@model=LKM614
@description=Plug-in IEC 62056-21 to Modbus RTU module for EMH LZQJ-XC meters (Variomod XC replacement), RS485 on the Modbus side
@source=REDZ, "LKM Series Electricity Meter Protocol to Modbus Protocol Gateways User Manual", sections 6.1, 6.5-6.10 and 8 (standard 24-register firmware)
@protocol=rtu
@unit_id=1
@baudrate=19200
@parity=N
@databits=8
@stopbits=1
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@enum_reading_method=0=Method 1: full table + BCC (obsolete)|1=Method 2: line by line

name,group,area,address,type,scale,offset,unit,access,write_min,write_max,bit,bits,enum,description
Time (0.9.1),Meter 1,holding,0,uint32,,,,R,,,,,,OBIS 0.9.1. hhmmss as digits (10:25:07 reads 102507). 0 if not in the read-out
Date (0.9.2),Meter 1,holding,2,uint32,,,,R,,,,,,OBIS 0.9.2. yymmdd as digits (22-09-14 reads 220914). 0 if not in the read-out
Active energy import A+ (1.8.0),Meter 1,holding,4,uint32,,,,R,,,,,,OBIS 1.8.0. Digits of the read-out value without the decimal point (e.g. 6895.2317 reads 68952317): apply the meter's decimals. 0 if not in the read-out
Active energy export A- (2.8.0),Meter 1,holding,6,uint32,,,,R,,,,,,OBIS 2.8.0. Digits of the read-out value without the decimal point (e.g. 6895.2317 reads 68952317): apply the meter's decimals. 0 if not in the read-out
